# The app's screens on the four colour platforms, from a wiped state, in the
# README's order: the list with a one-minute timer selected, that timer
# caught mid-run at 0:42 in the detail window, the settings with the Accent
# Color row selected, and the picker with Picton Blue chosen.
#
# The first three shots wear the shipped Malachite default; the accent is
# applied on the way to the picker, so the last shot is the only one in
# Picton Blue -- it is the shot about choosing it.
#
# The detail shot is taken while the timer is still running -- the pause
# glyph, not the play one, is what a live countdown looks like -- and it
# must say 0:42 with the status bar at 12:34. That pair can only exist on a
# clock pin's island: the countdown reads the wall clock, every capture
# pins that clock to 12:34:00, and pypkjs re-syncs it back to the machine's
# real time a couple of seconds after any pin -- a leaked tick lands the
# timer hours past zero (Time's Up!) before a CLI-paced chain finishes.
# fasttick therefore does the whole dance in one websocket session: pin
# 12:33:42, press start (the timer ends 12:34:42), re-pin 12:34:00 every
# 100ms across a redraw tick -- the re-sync deadline slides forward with
# every pin, so the island never dies -- and grab the frame: ~0:42, live.
# The pause press after it is insurance either way (SELECT also dismisses
# the expiry popup) and keeps the timer frozen for the walk to the settings
# shots. See tools/fasttick.py.
#
#   tools/screenshots.sh -p emery -w -t 12:34:00 -o tmp/shots/readme tools/scenes/readme-tour.scene

note the app opens straight to the duration picker when there are no timers
wait 4              # the app's first window needs to be up before presses land
note dial one minute
press select        # off hours
press up 1          # one minute
press select        # off minutes
press select        # confirm -- detail opens, not started
press back          # menu, cursor on the timer row
shot list           # the main list, 1:00 selected
note run it down to 42 seconds
press select        # open the timer
fasttick 12:33:42 select detail   # pin, start, hold, frame -- see the header
press select        # freeze the 0:42 (or dismiss if the island slipped)
press back          # menu
press down          # to the cog row
press select        # Settings
press down 2        # past the two group rows to Accent Color, the last row
shot settings       # the settings menu with the Accent Color row selected
press select        # the colour picker, opening on Malachite, the shipped default
note choose Picton Blue
press down          # to Picton Blue, next in the palette
press select        # apply -- pops back to settings, everything wears blue now
press select        # back into the picker, opening on the chosen colour
shot color          # the accent colour menu with Picton Blue selected
